      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hrmm, so this will only work if the reexec logic is executed.\n\nIs running zmake outside the chroot supported? Outside the chroot we can\u0027t rely on PYTHONPATH being anything sane.\n\ni.e., we can call `(outside) $ PYTHONPATH\u003d/tmp/foo zmake ....` and we will fail to lookup the toolchains.\n\nPYTHONPATH normally gets appended to the search path:\n```\n$ PYTHONPATH\u003d/foo:/bar python3 -c \u0027import sys; print(sys.path)\u0027\n[\u0027\u0027, \u0027/foo\u0027, \u0027/bar\u0027, \u0027/usr/lib/python311.zip\u0027, \u0027/usr/lib/python3.11\u0027, \u0027/usr/lib/python3.11/lib-dynload\u0027, \u0027/usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages\u0027, \u0027/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages\u0027, \u0027/usr/lib/python3.11/dist-packages\u0027]\n```\n\nIf anything I would put a comment here explaining what the expectation for PYTHONPATH is and why this works.",
      "parentUuid": "d2505199_fbf69165",
